1
00:00:00,576 --> 00:00:03,240
(Previously) You have been
charged with embezzling funds.

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:04,880
Dad! Grandma!

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,361
Phob, thank you

4
00:00:07,088 --> 00:00:08,120
for everything.

5
00:00:10,624 --> 00:00:12,625
I'll be looking forward
to seeing you succeed.

6
00:00:17,462 --> 00:00:18,880
Is selling this palace

7
00:00:19,259 --> 00:00:21,080
really our only option?

8
00:00:21,931 --> 00:00:24,624
Your Highness, I wish
you have a better life.

9
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,240
Sometimes I can't help but wonder...

10
00:00:32,496 --> 00:00:34,320
was everything I lost

11
00:00:34,678 --> 00:00:36,000
really worth it?

12
00:00:36,432 --> 00:00:37,560
I am rooting for you.

13
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:07,300
"The Edge of Horizon"
(Episode 10)

14
00:02:10,285 --> 00:02:11,286
Look at this.

15
00:02:15,952 --> 00:02:18,152
The government has ordered
another review of the press.

16
00:02:18,219 --> 00:02:20,530
Any newspaper that criticizes the government
too harshly gets summoned or shut down.

17
00:02:20,656 --> 00:02:22,903
[3 More Newspapers Ordered
to Shut Down; Is This Freedom?]

18
00:02:22,958 --> 00:02:25,719
Things are even more restrictive now
than they were before the revolution.

19
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,392
We fought to change this country

20
00:02:30,819 --> 00:02:33,000
because we wanted people
to have rights and freedoms.

21
00:02:33,443 --> 00:02:35,803
So tell me—how is this any different
from what came before?

22
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:44,984
It does make a difference.

23
00:02:53,352 --> 00:02:54,752
I've asked myself the same thing...

24
00:02:57,603 --> 00:03:01,255
whether what we did really
changed anything at all.

25
00:03:05,422 --> 00:03:07,176
But someone once told me that

26
00:03:09,875 --> 00:03:11,035
we may not see the difference

27
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:14,851
we've made in the grand scheme of things.

28
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:17,550
But in the lives of ordinary people,

29
00:03:18,376 --> 00:03:19,656
we've already made a difference.

30
00:03:24,486 --> 00:03:25,487
Maybe

31
00:03:26,816 --> 00:03:28,022
what we do

32
00:03:29,275 --> 00:03:31,451
can't change the whole world overnight.

33
00:03:32,403 --> 00:03:33,404
But at least

34
00:03:34,112 --> 00:03:35,670
it can change someone's life

35
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:37,859
and give them hope.

36
00:03:44,976 --> 00:03:46,536
Are you talking about Prince Tinnakorn?

37
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:52,160
It is that obvious?

38
00:03:54,696 --> 00:03:56,696
Ever since you came back
from the school that day,

39
00:03:57,747 --> 00:03:59,760
you've seemed more like yourself again.

40
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,110
Before I went to see him that day,

41
00:04:08,451 --> 00:04:11,920
I'd planned out everything I wanted to say.

42
00:04:13,507 --> 00:04:14,800
I wanted to tell him

43
00:04:16,088 --> 00:04:17,360
how deeply sorry I was.

44
00:04:20,462 --> 00:04:23,880
I wanted to beg him to let us
go back to the way we were.

45
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,680
But when the moment came,

46
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,280
I couldn't say a word.

47
00:04:33,678 --> 00:04:35,840
He seemed so much stronger than I was.

48
00:04:39,472 --> 00:04:41,000
What are you going to do?

49
00:04:43,019 --> 00:04:44,040
I don't know.

50
00:04:47,008 --> 00:04:49,109
I'm not hoping for things

51
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:50,870
to go back to the way they were.

52
00:04:52,827 --> 00:04:53,987
But if I ever get the chance,

53
00:04:56,608 --> 00:04:59,880
I hope he'll open up to
me again, even just a little.

54
00:05:02,688 --> 00:05:04,500
I still want to walk beside him,

55
00:05:06,979 --> 00:05:08,480
and I never want to hurt him again.

56
00:05:14,499 --> 00:05:15,768
I once chose my belief

57
00:05:18,584 --> 00:05:20,864
over the person I loved most,
and I ended up hurting him.

58
00:05:22,702 --> 00:05:23,703
From now on,

59
00:05:26,046 --> 00:05:27,280
if I'm given another chance,

60
00:05:30,518 --> 00:05:32,120
I want to make him proud

61
00:05:35,248 --> 00:05:36,760
instead of causing him more pain.

62
00:05:54,374 --> 00:05:56,000
What are you planting?

63
00:05:59,347 --> 00:06:02,579
Oh, it's cotton rose tree.
Where did you get it?

64
00:06:03,236 --> 00:06:06,024
The principal planted
several of them at school,

65
00:06:06,638 --> 00:06:08,840
so I asked if I could have
one to plant here at home.

66
00:06:13,198 --> 00:06:14,800
You miss him, don't you?

67
00:06:22,219 --> 00:06:23,936
Trees are remarkable, aren't they?

68
00:06:24,566 --> 00:06:26,480
No matter where they're transplanted,

69
00:06:26,747 --> 00:06:29,280
as long as their roots remain strong,

70
00:06:30,107 --> 00:06:33,560
they'll grow again before long.

71
00:06:35,571 --> 00:06:37,440
Perhaps trees are luckier than people.

72
00:06:39,147 --> 00:06:41,915
Give them soil and water,
and they can grow again.

73
00:06:43,936 --> 00:06:45,320
But people are different.

74
00:06:46,587 --> 00:06:49,187
No matter how much we may wish to
go back to the way things were,

75
00:06:50,091 --> 00:06:51,691
some things can never be the same again.

76
00:06:57,611 --> 00:06:59,958
Who says things have to be the same?

77
00:07:00,592 --> 00:07:04,208
People are strange, aren't they?

78
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:07,099
Why do we always think
our lives, our happiness,

79
00:07:07,136 --> 00:07:09,840
have to stay the same forever?

80
00:07:10,910 --> 00:07:15,100
Take the things we own, for example.
When something gets broken

81
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,401
or damaged,

82
00:07:16,968 --> 00:07:20,000
it may never work the way it used to.

83
00:07:20,454 --> 00:07:23,355
But that doesn't mean
it can't still be good.

84
00:07:26,011 --> 00:07:27,012
Grandma?

85
00:07:30,891 --> 00:07:33,360
I want to tell you about life.

86
00:07:33,814 --> 00:07:37,558
Life isn't about trying to
hold on to the same happiness

87
00:07:38,032 --> 00:07:40,920
and success forever.

88
00:07:42,496 --> 00:07:46,363
Listen to me. What
matters most is learning…

89
00:07:47,254 --> 00:07:48,760
to accept

90
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,123
and understand

91
00:07:51,832 --> 00:07:53,934
the things that change,

92
00:07:55,011 --> 00:07:56,360
to live with those changes…

93
00:07:57,752 --> 00:07:59,089
with grace,

94
00:08:00,142 --> 00:08:01,920
and to make the best of what we have.

95
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:03,991
Okay?

96
00:08:04,739 --> 00:08:05,740
Okay.

97
00:08:12,696 --> 00:08:14,400
Thank you so much.

98
00:08:22,182 --> 00:08:23,440
Grandma! Grandma!

99
00:08:25,301 --> 00:08:26,802
- Grandma?
- Your Highness?

100
00:08:27,174 --> 00:08:28,760
Let's get her inside. Grandma?

101
00:08:33,302 --> 00:08:35,824
Grandma, maybe we
should go to the hospital.

102
00:08:36,171 --> 00:08:37,680
Oh, I don't have to.

103
00:08:38,112 --> 00:08:41,600
That's just what happens when you get old.
You get a little dizzy now and then.

104
00:08:41,752 --> 00:08:43,800
I'll be fine after a bit of rest.

105
00:08:44,163 --> 00:08:46,040
But you don't look fine to me.

106
00:08:47,246 --> 00:08:50,800
Should I contact Chat and Dad?

107
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:53,120
No need to.

108
00:08:53,302 --> 00:08:55,771
We don't have to trouble them.

109
00:08:56,187 --> 00:08:59,627
They already have a lot on their plates.

110
00:09:01,579 --> 00:09:02,580
Grandma?

111
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:06,128
Oh, I know why I got lightheaded.

112
00:09:06,502 --> 00:09:08,230
I must be hungry.

113
00:09:08,699 --> 00:09:10,600
The desserts sold so well today

114
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:12,862
that I got busy and forgot to eat.

115
00:09:13,534 --> 00:09:17,011
I knew it! You had me so worried.

116
00:09:17,166 --> 00:09:18,760
That's why I told you

117
00:09:18,952 --> 00:09:21,240
to stop and get something
to eat at the market first.

118
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:24,030
You'd better watch yourself, Aum!

119
00:09:24,579 --> 00:09:28,280
Stop talking and finding
me something to eat.

120
00:09:29,411 --> 00:09:30,720
- Sure.
- I'm starving.

121
00:09:31,998 --> 00:09:36,111
The desserts were selling so well today
that I got too busy to eat.

122
00:09:36,312 --> 00:09:38,600
Let me lie down for a bit. I'll be fine.

123
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,080
Then I'll go prepare some
herbal medicine for you.

124
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,246
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

125
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:10,281
No! No!

126
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,800
The forces that will join us…

127
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,050
are from Ubon Ratchathani, Nakhon Sawan,

128
00:10:16,312 --> 00:10:18,720
Prachin Buri, Ratchaburi, and Phetchaburi.

129
00:10:19,342 --> 00:10:21,032
But I still have my doubts.

130
00:10:21,437 --> 00:10:24,464
We don't know whether the units that
pledged their support will actually join us.

131
00:10:24,488 --> 00:10:26,676
Many of them are reluctant
to fight their own countrymen.

132
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:27,720
Their own side?

133
00:10:29,238 --> 00:10:31,336
Ever since they seized power,
they've driven our people…

134
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,528
out of government service and
imprisoned members of the royal family.

135
00:10:35,616 --> 00:10:37,900
They turned those who had
served this country their entire lives

136
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,299
into enemies of the state.

137
00:10:42,366 --> 00:10:44,766
They stopped seeing us as
their own a long time ago.

138
00:10:46,457 --> 00:10:48,280
Today they silence the press.

139
00:10:48,879 --> 00:10:51,159
Tomorrow, they'll silence anyone
who disagrees with them.

140
00:10:51,358 --> 00:10:52,918
And one day, what will be left of Siam?

141
00:10:55,171 --> 00:10:57,680
I will not stand by and watch Siam

142
00:10:57,882 --> 00:10:59,630
be led down the wrong path.

143
00:11:00,051 --> 00:11:01,400
I agree with you, Your Highness.

144
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,694
Even if they brand me a traitor, so be it.

145
00:11:04,104 --> 00:11:05,600
This is no rebellion.

146
00:11:06,696 --> 00:11:08,800
We are fighting to reclaim our country.

147
00:11:09,814 --> 00:11:11,646
If we do not rise up today,

148
00:11:12,096 --> 00:11:14,850
there may be no country
left for us to defend tomorrow.

149
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:29,000
Why are you setting up the
shop yourself? Where is Aum?

150
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:32,720
Oh, I asked Aum to buy
food for me. I'm quite hungry.

151
00:11:34,755 --> 00:11:36,000
I'll leave you to it.

152
00:11:38,931 --> 00:11:40,723
Khanom Jeen is here.

153
00:11:42,024 --> 00:11:43,520
They look so good.

154
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:47,362
We have steamed banana cakes
and coconut-filled sweets today.

155
00:11:47,413 --> 00:11:49,640
- Which one do you want?
- I'll take three of these.

156
00:11:49,808 --> 00:11:52,000
One bag of this one, this one…and that one.

157
00:11:53,622 --> 00:11:55,256
- I'll put them in the bags for you.
- Let me check on chicken.

158
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,320
- Sure.
- Okay.

159
00:11:59,512 --> 00:12:01,120
Your Highness!

160
00:12:03,579 --> 00:12:04,580
Your Highness!

161
00:12:04,958 --> 00:12:07,080
Please help! She passed out!

162
00:12:11,024 --> 00:12:12,920
She passed out! Please help!

163
00:12:14,572 --> 00:12:15,892
- Princess.
- She passed out, sir.

164
00:12:16,491 --> 00:12:17,571
Let me help you get her up.

165
00:12:18,411 --> 00:12:19,412
Your Highness!

166
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:22,521
Easy there.

167
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,721
[Siamvejsathan Hospital]

168
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,561
[Emergency Room]

169
00:12:46,055 --> 00:12:47,056
How is my grandma?

170
00:12:48,369 --> 00:12:49,640
The doctor hasn't come out yet.

171
00:12:50,739 --> 00:12:51,740
Where is Aum?

172
00:12:52,339 --> 00:12:54,179
She's in the room with
Princess Patthamapriya.

173
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:59,440
How did this happen?
She was fine this morning.

174
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,440
Please calm down.

175
00:13:02,241 --> 00:13:03,680
Your grandma will be okay.

176
00:13:11,758 --> 00:13:13,838
- Has the patient's family arrived yet?
- I'm here.

177
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,320
The doctor would like to
see you. This way, please.

178
00:13:26,374 --> 00:13:29,160
She is now suffering from kidney failure.

179
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,600
Toxins are building up in her blood,

180
00:13:32,056 --> 00:13:34,120
and her electrolytes
are severely imbalanced.

181
00:13:34,694 --> 00:13:36,934
At this point, all we can do
is provide supportive care.

182
00:13:37,395 --> 00:13:41,080
The rest depends on how her body responds.

183
00:13:41,424 --> 00:13:42,680
What do you mean?

184
00:13:43,782 --> 00:13:45,320
Will she recover soon?

185
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,040
- For how long?
- Aum.

186
00:13:49,101 --> 00:13:51,160
Stop yelling already.

187
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,240
You're always embarrassing me.

188
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,040
Well, I am worried
about you, Your Highness.

189
00:13:57,600 --> 00:14:00,320
I heard the doctor but I didn't get it.

190
00:14:02,203 --> 00:14:03,680
Did you get it, Phob?

191
00:14:10,806 --> 00:14:12,120
It's okay, Grandma.

192
00:14:12,747 --> 00:14:15,280
The doctor will heal you,
you will get better soon.

193
00:14:29,576 --> 00:14:30,720
Please be careful.

194
00:14:33,283 --> 00:14:34,284
Walk slowly.

195
00:14:35,688 --> 00:14:36,689
Have a seat, please.

196
00:14:45,147 --> 00:14:48,176
Auntie, please find
something for her to eat.

197
00:14:48,443 --> 00:14:50,145
- So she can take her medicine.
- Okay.

198
00:14:50,374 --> 00:14:53,600
She needs to take the medicine
the doctor prescribed on time.

199
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,180
The doctor will see her again in two weeks.

200
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,646
I will come and take her to the hospital.

201
00:14:57,670 --> 00:14:59,680
Oh, you don't have to.

202
00:15:00,075 --> 00:15:02,120
I can take her, I don't want to bother you.

203
00:15:02,424 --> 00:15:03,920
You won't be bothering me.

204
00:15:04,812 --> 00:15:06,372
Please let me take her to the hospital.

205
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:08,160
But I think I should...

206
00:15:08,321 --> 00:15:10,520
Thank you so much, Phob.

207
00:16:12,854 --> 00:16:13,855
Phob.

208
00:16:21,571 --> 00:16:24,840
This is for the medicine
and the doctor's fee today.

209
00:16:25,379 --> 00:16:27,059
Thank you for today. Here, please take it.

210
00:16:31,726 --> 00:16:33,600
I don't think I can take it.

211
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:35,391
You should take it.

212
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:40,280
You've already done more than enough
just by taking her to the doctor.

213
00:16:40,824 --> 00:16:42,344
It's no trouble at all, Your Highness.

214
00:16:43,307 --> 00:16:46,400
I owe her more than I could ever repay.

215
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:52,520
This is the least I can do.

216
00:17:00,832 --> 00:17:01,833
Thank you.

217
00:17:11,427 --> 00:17:13,180
Are you okay, Your Highness?

218
00:17:21,416 --> 00:17:22,417
I'm scared.

219
00:17:24,013 --> 00:17:25,760
I'm scared I'm gonna lose my grandma.

220
00:17:27,787 --> 00:17:29,640
I should have noticed her symptoms sooner.

221
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:33,440
So I could take her to the
hospital, to see the doctor.

222
00:17:35,814 --> 00:17:37,240
Why can't I do anything?

223
00:17:37,483 --> 00:17:38,840
I couldn't save anyone.

224
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,680
I'm scared that I will be left alone.

225
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,300
What if I have to be alone?

226
00:17:52,886 --> 00:17:53,887
Phob?

227
00:18:19,830 --> 00:18:20,840
It's okay, Your Highness.

228
00:18:24,827 --> 00:18:25,920
Your Phob is here for you.

229
00:18:39,195 --> 00:18:40,196
Phob.

230
00:18:42,928 --> 00:18:44,040
Morning, dear.

231
00:18:45,168 --> 00:18:46,169
Let me help you.

232
00:19:20,992 --> 00:19:22,993
[Pharmacy]

233
00:19:32,798 --> 00:19:35,840
Take one tablet three times a day—
morning, noon, and evening,

234
00:19:38,202 --> 00:19:39,642
This one is to be taken after meals.

235
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:40,960
Ew, it's so bitter.

236
00:19:42,763 --> 00:19:44,240
This is a good stuff, Your Highness.

237
00:19:44,491 --> 00:19:45,800
Then you eat it.

238
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,601
It's too bitter.

239
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:55,280
Have some candied jujube to take away
the bitter taste, Your Highness.

240
00:19:56,352 --> 00:19:58,440
Thank you, Phob.

241
00:20:03,646 --> 00:20:04,720
Oh, it's better.

242
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,840
Phob, the cotton rose we
planted has finally bloomed.

243
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:37,523
Please be careful.

244
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:42,280
Please slow down.

245
00:21:43,664 --> 00:21:46,920
I'm going to trip and fall because of you!

246
00:21:47,046 --> 00:21:50,800
You keep darting back and forth
in front of me. So annoying.

247
00:21:51,116 --> 00:21:53,236
It's slippery here, Your Highness.
Please be careful.

248
00:21:54,054 --> 00:21:55,400
Just leave me alone.

249
00:21:55,606 --> 00:21:56,840
Please be careful.

250
00:22:14,907 --> 00:22:15,960
Phob?

251
00:22:19,784 --> 00:22:21,720
What brings you here?

252
00:22:22,627 --> 00:22:25,628
It's not time for my checkup yet, is it?

253
00:22:28,206 --> 00:22:29,886
Someone is here to see you, Your Highness.

254
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:32,301
Who?

255
00:22:53,587 --> 00:22:54,588
Nual?

256
00:23:02,454 --> 00:23:05,160
Oh, Nual. Get up.

257
00:23:07,455 --> 00:23:08,920
It's you. It really is you.

258
00:23:13,542 --> 00:23:14,843
I missed you.

259
00:23:16,982 --> 00:23:17,983
I missed you.

260
00:23:33,275 --> 00:23:35,360
You shouldn't have to live like this.

261
00:23:36,448 --> 00:23:37,449
This is all

262
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:39,801
because of Phob.

263
00:23:43,312 --> 00:23:46,485
Look at what you've done!

264
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,790
She used to live in comfort,

265
00:23:50,419 --> 00:23:51,420
and now look at her...

266
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,680
It's okay. Don't yell at him.

267
00:23:54,472 --> 00:23:57,320
Phob, why don't you
help Aum put things away?

268
00:23:57,707 --> 00:24:00,180
You bought so many things.

269
00:24:09,494 --> 00:24:12,280
Nual, come sit up here with me.

270
00:24:14,704 --> 00:24:16,184
It wouldn't be proper, Your Highness.

271
00:24:16,705 --> 00:24:18,120
Oh, it's all right.

272
00:24:18,398 --> 00:24:21,581
There's no such thing as
proper or improper anymore.

273
00:24:21,726 --> 00:24:23,480
Come here.

274
00:24:23,550 --> 00:24:26,760
Come sit with me. Make
yourself comfortable.

275
00:24:28,323 --> 00:24:29,420
Come on.

276
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:45,121
I…

277
00:24:46,616 --> 00:24:48,250
I failed as a mother.

278
00:24:49,755 --> 00:24:51,880
If I'd raised him better,

279
00:24:56,016 --> 00:24:58,720
none of this would've
happened, Your Highness.

280
00:24:58,740 --> 00:25:01,720
Stop it, don't blame him.

281
00:25:03,091 --> 00:25:04,092
Your Highness.

282
00:25:05,352 --> 00:25:07,193
Aren't you angry at Phob for what he did?

283
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:08,921
Of course I'm angry.

284
00:25:09,921 --> 00:25:13,320
And I'm deeply hurt.

285
00:25:14,251 --> 00:25:17,160
But what's happening now goes

286
00:25:17,872 --> 00:25:20,280
far beyond Phob.

287
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:23,100
Even if he had never been involved,

288
00:25:23,966 --> 00:25:25,401
sooner or later,

289
00:25:25,987 --> 00:25:28,460
something like this would
have happened anyway.

290
00:25:28,526 --> 00:25:30,680
But Phob still shouldn't have...

291
00:25:31,670 --> 00:25:33,680
shouldn't have sided with those people.

292
00:25:35,376 --> 00:25:38,160
He should've remembered everything
your family had done for him.

293
00:25:38,310 --> 00:25:40,320
He does.

294
00:25:41,126 --> 00:25:45,560
If he didn't, he wouldn't
be suffering this much.

295
00:25:46,998 --> 00:25:48,560
But we have to understand

296
00:25:49,366 --> 00:25:52,040
that young people today

297
00:25:52,443 --> 00:25:54,440
see life differently from our generation.

298
00:25:55,216 --> 00:25:56,760
We look to the past,

299
00:25:58,051 --> 00:26:00,040
while they look to the future.

300
00:26:00,432 --> 00:26:02,640
They don't see things

301
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,360
in terms of who was right or wrong.

302
00:26:06,070 --> 00:26:07,200
All they know

303
00:26:08,056 --> 00:26:11,240
is that they're willing
to sacrifice everything

304
00:26:11,488 --> 00:26:15,400
for what they believe in.

305
00:26:18,166 --> 00:26:19,680
And perhaps,

306
00:26:20,339 --> 00:26:22,080
in the end,

307
00:26:23,280 --> 00:26:25,960
it's we who have to learn to let go.

308
00:26:31,091 --> 00:26:32,092
Nual,

309
00:26:32,792 --> 00:26:35,080
the same goes for you.

310
00:26:35,677 --> 00:26:37,720
You need to learn to let go, too,

311
00:26:38,254 --> 00:26:40,000
of everything

312
00:26:40,443 --> 00:26:42,640
that's happening now,

313
00:26:42,939 --> 00:26:44,400
and even what happened

314
00:26:46,795 --> 00:26:49,120
between Phob and Tin.

315
00:26:52,451 --> 00:26:53,452
Your Highness?

316
00:26:55,096 --> 00:26:57,240
You knew about this?

317
00:26:59,256 --> 00:27:00,357
You must have known

318
00:27:01,136 --> 00:27:04,440
about it for a long
time too, haven't you?

319
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:07,520
That's why you took
him away from the palace.

320
00:27:10,992 --> 00:27:11,993
That's right.

321
00:27:14,475 --> 00:27:16,440
I was trying to stop him.

322
00:27:18,120 --> 00:27:20,100
That's why I got Phob out of the palace.

323
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:23,120
But in the end,

324
00:27:24,624 --> 00:27:26,200
none of it made any difference.

325
00:27:31,014 --> 00:27:33,280
I used to think the same thing...

326
00:27:34,575 --> 00:27:38,680
that if those two hadn't fallen in love,

327
00:27:39,147 --> 00:27:40,760
everything

328
00:27:41,220 --> 00:27:43,320
might have been easier.

329
00:27:44,744 --> 00:27:48,700
But as time went by,

330
00:27:49,923 --> 00:27:52,120
I stopped thinking that way.

331
00:27:55,080 --> 00:27:56,520
Do you know why, Nual?

332
00:27:57,902 --> 00:28:00,050
Because…

333
00:28:00,744 --> 00:28:02,160
life is short.

334
00:28:03,166 --> 00:28:07,161
Far too short for us

335
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:10,640
to waste it deciding who should love whom,

336
00:28:10,792 --> 00:28:13,480
or trying to tell people

337
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:16,400
who they should or shouldn't be with.

338
00:28:21,054 --> 00:28:23,280
And the same goes for you, Nual.

339
00:28:23,800 --> 00:28:25,801
If those two ever

340
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:28,750
find their way back to each other,

341
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,720
let them.

342
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:34,520
Let go and stay out of it.

343
00:28:35,043 --> 00:28:36,640
It's their life.

344
00:28:37,528 --> 00:28:40,440
Let them choose for themselves.

345
00:28:43,006 --> 00:28:45,440
- But I'm scared...
- I know. I know.

346
00:28:45,550 --> 00:28:47,320
I know. I get it.

347
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:49,920
I understand your fear.

348
00:28:50,206 --> 00:28:53,000
But don't let your fear

349
00:28:53,454 --> 00:28:57,806
become a cage for those two.

350
00:29:24,976 --> 00:29:26,160
Did you see her?

351
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:29,480
She looked so tired and weak.

352
00:29:32,800 --> 00:29:34,920
I never wanted her to suffer.

353
00:29:37,286 --> 00:29:39,040
I never wanted any of this to happen.

354
00:29:40,902 --> 00:29:42,822
I feel guilty for what
I've put you all through.

355
00:29:45,022 --> 00:29:48,760
From now on, try to visit her more often.

356
00:29:49,715 --> 00:29:53,160
And if there's anything we can do for her,

357
00:29:54,254 --> 00:29:55,320
let's do what we can.

358
00:29:56,462 --> 00:29:57,463
Sure, Mom.

359
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:14,100
Take care of yourself too.

360
00:30:17,811 --> 00:30:19,251
You've lost so much weight, my dear.

361
00:31:08,704 --> 00:31:09,705
Dad.

362
00:31:15,678 --> 00:31:17,400
When did you come back?

363
00:31:18,220 --> 00:31:19,360
I just arrived this morning.

364
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:22,680
I have some business to
take care of in the capital.

365
00:31:24,396 --> 00:31:26,120
But I probably won't be staying at home.

366
00:31:26,854 --> 00:31:28,200
I have quite a few things to do,

367
00:31:28,987 --> 00:31:31,107
so it'll be more convenient
for me to stay with Adul.

368
00:31:31,408 --> 00:31:33,080
Where is Chat?

369
00:31:34,555 --> 00:31:35,835
He's still in Nakhon Ratchasima.

370
00:31:36,787 --> 00:31:38,700
There're a lot for us to take care of.

371
00:31:43,694 --> 00:31:45,440
I heard that you were sick.

372
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,121
How are you feeling?

373
00:31:47,288 --> 00:31:50,160
- Her health...
- I went to see the doctor already.

374
00:31:50,536 --> 00:31:54,160
The doctor gave me some medicine.

375
00:31:54,424 --> 00:31:56,104
I'll be better in no time. I'm fine, dear.

376
00:31:58,667 --> 00:31:59,680
I will be fine.

377
00:32:05,659 --> 00:32:07,120
You've lost so much weight.

378
00:32:09,296 --> 00:32:10,976
Things must have been really hard for you.

379
00:32:12,048 --> 00:32:13,480
It hasn't been easy,

380
00:32:14,454 --> 00:32:15,880
but I'm getting by.

381
00:32:17,454 --> 00:32:18,480
Hang in there, Tin.

382
00:32:19,624 --> 00:32:22,360
It won't be long before
everything goes back to the way it was.

383
00:32:24,472 --> 00:32:26,160
What do you mean?

384
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:29,160
You'll know when the time comes.

385
00:32:44,702 --> 00:32:47,680
We have submitted an application to
register a political association

386
00:32:47,950 --> 00:32:49,800
under the name 'Free Siam Movement.'

387
00:32:50,232 --> 00:32:52,880
Our guiding principles are

388
00:32:53,150 --> 00:32:54,880
to uphold democracy

389
00:32:55,139 --> 00:32:58,960
and to preserve, for all time,
the constitutional monarchy

390
00:32:59,072 --> 00:33:01,640
with the King as Head of State.

391
00:33:04,059 --> 00:33:06,760
Is this application to
establish a political association

392
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:09,600
intended to rival the
Khana Ratsadon Association?

393
00:33:11,699 --> 00:33:14,601
We believe that our country
has now become an oligarchy,

394
00:33:14,894 --> 00:33:17,662
ruled by a small group that seized power.

395
00:33:17,944 --> 00:33:20,880
The people have yet to enjoy true freedom,

396
00:33:21,443 --> 00:33:23,840
and this is a danger we must guard against.

397
00:33:24,104 --> 00:33:27,360
We therefore call upon
all citizens to join us.

398
00:33:27,811 --> 00:33:31,200
Do you think people will join your group?

399
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:35,081
[Free Siam Movement Launched]

400
00:33:35,100 --> 00:33:37,101
[Vows to Revive the Economy, Safeguard
Independence, and Uphold the Constitution]

401
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:39,400
[Unveils Its Principles to
the Public for the First Time]

402
00:33:41,382 --> 00:33:44,600
It looks like Prince
Vasin is serious this time.

403
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:49,400
If this were just about
forming a political association,

404
00:33:50,195 --> 00:33:52,600
I wouldn't be this concerned.

405
00:33:53,582 --> 00:33:55,862
Our sources report unusual activity
in Nakhon Ratchasima.

406
00:33:56,051 --> 00:33:57,052
Activities?

407
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,001
How?

408
00:33:59,616 --> 00:34:02,120
They've been contacting
several military units,

409
00:34:02,496 --> 00:34:05,480
holding secret meetings,
and rallying supporters.

410
00:34:05,846 --> 00:34:07,640
We're keeping a close watch to see

411
00:34:08,054 --> 00:34:09,600
which factions are joining them.

412
00:34:11,270 --> 00:34:14,560
If that's true, it could lead
to an armed confrontation.

413
00:34:18,923 --> 00:34:20,280
I don't want that to happen.

414
00:34:20,706 --> 00:34:22,346
We've spent years talking about democracy

415
00:34:22,536 --> 00:34:23,960
and the future of our country.

416
00:34:25,028 --> 00:34:26,029
If, in the end,

417
00:34:26,968 --> 00:34:28,800
it all has to be decided by bullets,

418
00:34:31,717 --> 00:34:32,880
that would be a tragedy.

419
00:34:54,857 --> 00:34:56,040
How is it?

420
00:34:56,807 --> 00:35:00,320
Very good. With a few minor revisions,
it should be ready for publication.

421
00:35:00,898 --> 00:35:03,040
- Really?
- Yes.

422
00:35:03,591 --> 00:35:05,040
I'll see if I can find
the right opportunity

423
00:35:05,060 --> 00:35:07,661
to publish it as a serial in the magazine.

424
00:35:08,864 --> 00:35:12,280
You're so talented and you
should be proud of yourself.

425
00:35:14,928 --> 00:35:18,080
I want my father to be proud of me.

426
00:35:19,032 --> 00:35:22,926
I want him to see that
what I'm doing has value.

427
00:35:23,379 --> 00:35:25,040
It may take some time.

428
00:35:26,446 --> 00:35:28,120
Your father's generation

429
00:35:28,456 --> 00:35:30,960
isn't used to seeing women
pursue careers of their own.

430
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:35,440
But one day, he'll see
just how capable you are.

431
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:44,200
The Free Siam Movement held
a public gathering in the capital,

432
00:35:44,462 --> 00:35:47,960
where Prince Vasin delivered a speech.

433
00:35:58,110 --> 00:36:02,640
Are you concerned about
the Free Siam Movement?

434
00:36:03,512 --> 00:36:05,920
I've been hearing so
much about them lately.

435
00:36:08,224 --> 00:36:10,680
Until now, we've been fortunate
enough to avoid bloodshed.

436
00:36:11,696 --> 00:36:13,720
But if force is used this time,

437
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:17,401
I fear it may end very differently.

438
00:36:17,654 --> 00:36:18,800
Is it really that serious?

439
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:24,600
I don't know much about politics,

440
00:36:25,120 --> 00:36:27,000
but I don't want anyone to die.

441
00:36:29,416 --> 00:36:31,136
We're all from the same country, after all.

442
00:36:43,680 --> 00:36:44,681
[Free Siam Movement Launched]

443
00:36:44,700 --> 00:36:47,940
[Vows to Revive the Economy, Safeguard
Independence, and Uphold the Constitution]

444
00:36:53,374 --> 00:36:54,375
Dad?

445
00:36:56,067 --> 00:36:57,068
Where is your grandma?

446
00:36:58,056 --> 00:37:00,920
She went to the hospital with Aum,
she will be back soon.

447
00:37:07,395 --> 00:37:09,320
I saw the news about
the Free Siam Movement.

448
00:37:15,736 --> 00:37:18,120
I'm going to fight to
reclaim Siam from them.

449
00:37:18,958 --> 00:37:21,920
They need to know that
not everyone in Siam will bow to them.

450
00:37:23,262 --> 00:37:24,840
I don't want you to do this.

451
00:37:25,957 --> 00:37:27,280
I have a bad feeling about it.

452
00:37:28,848 --> 00:37:29,920
Don't worry about me.

453
00:37:30,667 --> 00:37:33,480
Chat and I didn't do this alone.

454
00:37:33,877 --> 00:37:35,100
We still have the support

455
00:37:35,246 --> 00:37:37,720
of many members of the royal family.

456
00:37:38,400 --> 00:37:40,840
I don't want any unrest.

457
00:37:41,160 --> 00:37:42,900
I just want our country to be at peace.

458
00:37:42,961 --> 00:37:44,761
They're the ones who
caused all this turmoil.

459
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:47,281
They're hungry for power,

460
00:37:48,081 --> 00:37:50,038
and they've torn apart
the order of this country.

461
00:37:50,062 --> 00:37:52,360
We cannot stand by and let
our nation continue like this.

462
00:37:52,526 --> 00:37:55,640
Maybe what they've done isn't really
as bad as it seems, Dad.

463
00:37:57,358 --> 00:37:58,359
What did you just say?

464
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:00,675
I used to think the same way you do.

465
00:38:01,671 --> 00:38:03,000
I was angry with them.

466
00:38:05,230 --> 00:38:08,120
I thought they had taken
everything away from us.

467
00:38:09,379 --> 00:38:12,400
But now that I've actually
lived outside the palace

468
00:38:13,566 --> 00:38:15,360
and seen how ordinary people live...

469
00:38:17,240 --> 00:38:18,640
Dad, some of my students

470
00:38:19,603 --> 00:38:20,680
are nearly twenty

471
00:38:21,405 --> 00:38:24,040
and still can't read or write.

472
00:38:25,736 --> 00:38:28,622
Some families have only just been able to
afford to send their children to school

473
00:38:28,646 --> 00:38:30,520
after several taxes were abolished.

474
00:38:33,499 --> 00:38:34,500
Is it because of him?

475
00:38:35,963 --> 00:38:37,400
He brainwashed you.

476
00:38:37,584 --> 00:38:40,185
- It has nothing to do with Phob...
- Of course it has!

477
00:38:42,038 --> 00:38:43,520
He's always been around.

478
00:38:44,584 --> 00:38:47,240
He hates me for keeping him away from you.

479
00:38:48,048 --> 00:38:49,920
That's why he came back to destroy us,

480
00:38:50,904 --> 00:38:54,160
to destroy our honor and our family name.

481
00:38:55,019 --> 00:38:57,720
Phob has never acted for his own gain.

482
00:38:58,080 --> 00:38:59,081
He may have been wrong.

483
00:39:00,270 --> 00:39:01,840
He may have made mistakes.

484
00:39:03,080 --> 00:39:04,881
But one thing I'm certain of is that

485
00:39:04,910 --> 00:39:07,600
he has never meant any harm to our country.

486
00:39:07,640 --> 00:39:08,920
You're defending him?

487
00:39:12,013 --> 00:39:15,040
After everything he's
done to you? He used you.

488
00:39:16,552 --> 00:39:19,000
He used your love for him as a weapon.

489
00:39:19,053 --> 00:39:20,160
He destroyed our family.

490
00:39:20,659 --> 00:39:23,200
And after all that, you still love him?

491
00:39:32,701 --> 00:39:33,702
Fine.

492
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:37,121
No matter how much you still love him,

493
00:39:37,728 --> 00:39:39,888
you can't stop me from
fighting for what I believe in.

494
00:39:40,987 --> 00:39:42,481
And I'm not alone anymore.

495
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:47,280
Forces from several provinces
are gathering as we speak.

496
00:39:47,723 --> 00:39:50,800
Those who love this country
are preparing to rise and fight.

497
00:39:51,467 --> 00:39:54,600
Before long, everything
will be the way it was again.

498
00:39:56,347 --> 00:39:57,680
What are you going to do?

499
00:40:20,616 --> 00:40:21,617
Phob.

500
00:40:22,462 --> 00:40:23,463
Have a seat.

501
00:40:24,499 --> 00:40:25,500
Yes, Your Highness.

502
00:40:31,715 --> 00:40:33,800
Why did you

503
00:40:34,600 --> 00:40:36,200
suddenly ask me to meet you out here?

504
00:40:36,712 --> 00:40:38,920
It's dangerous for you to
come out alone like this.

505
00:40:39,651 --> 00:40:41,280
Oh, I'm fine.

506
00:40:41,571 --> 00:40:44,040
I can still get around on my own.

507
00:40:44,307 --> 00:40:48,480
You're acting as if I'm going
to drop dead any day now.

508
00:40:51,310 --> 00:40:55,320
You know about Vasin's plan, don't you?

509
00:40:58,294 --> 00:40:59,295
I know about it.

510
00:41:01,366 --> 00:41:05,840
How are things in the country now?

511
00:41:06,379 --> 00:41:07,760
Is the situation serious?

512
00:41:12,165 --> 00:41:13,520
I've received word

513
00:41:14,651 --> 00:41:16,771
that the situation is very
concerning, Your Highness.

514
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:19,920
Troops are being mobilized,
alliances are being formed,

515
00:41:20,347 --> 00:41:22,427
and several factions have
begun making preparations.

516
00:41:22,741 --> 00:41:23,941
If we can't stop this in time,

517
00:41:24,912 --> 00:41:26,432
there could be an armed confrontation.

518
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:27,661
Oh my goodness.

519
00:41:29,011 --> 00:41:31,203
It is that serious?

520
00:41:33,864 --> 00:41:34,865
That's right.

521
00:41:35,710 --> 00:41:36,761
I didn't expect

522
00:41:38,478 --> 00:41:40,880
any of this to happen.

523
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:44,641
We can't be so sure anymore.

524
00:41:50,286 --> 00:41:51,720
- Your Highness.
- Phob.

525
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:55,240
If that day really comes,

526
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:58,600
there's something I want to ask of you.

527
00:41:59,410 --> 00:42:00,440
What is it?

528
00:42:03,259 --> 00:42:07,900
Please, don't be too
harsh on Vasin or Chat.

529
00:42:08,483 --> 00:42:10,560
I know,

530
00:42:10,947 --> 00:42:14,520
I understand that you're on opposing sides.

531
00:42:17,731 --> 00:42:19,320
But whatever happens,

532
00:42:20,700 --> 00:42:22,200
Vasin is still my son,

533
00:42:23,059 --> 00:42:25,201
and Chat is still my grandson.

534
00:42:33,040 --> 00:42:34,480
You needn't even ask, Your Highness.

535
00:42:36,470 --> 00:42:39,920
I would never harm
Prince Vasin or Prince Chat.

536
00:42:43,035 --> 00:42:45,160
Thank you so much.

537
00:42:47,632 --> 00:42:53,400
Vasin and Tinakorn had
an argument yesterday,

538
00:42:55,633 --> 00:42:57,920
over the very thing
we're talking about now.

539
00:43:00,990 --> 00:43:03,680
What did Prince Tinnakorn say?

540
00:43:04,464 --> 00:43:08,400
Tin said that not everything you've done

541
00:43:09,328 --> 00:43:12,000
is necessarily wrong.

542
00:43:12,917 --> 00:43:14,840
He knows you care about this country.

543
00:43:16,198 --> 00:43:19,280
You're simply doing
what you believe is right.

544
00:43:27,581 --> 00:43:29,101
Even after everything that's happened,

545
00:43:30,430 --> 00:43:31,880
he still defends me.

546
00:43:34,798 --> 00:43:35,840
And yet I'm the one

547
00:43:37,315 --> 00:43:38,441
who hurt him,

548
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:41,320
who caused him so much pain.

549
00:43:44,435 --> 00:43:45,640
I don't deserve

550
00:43:46,899 --> 00:43:48,920
the kindness he's shown me.

551
00:43:52,539 --> 00:43:56,840
I've watched the two
of you grow up together.

552
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:03,800
I know just
how much you mean to each other.

553
00:44:06,416 --> 00:44:08,200
But I destroyed that bond

554
00:44:09,702 --> 00:44:11,080
with my own hands.

555
00:44:11,703 --> 00:44:14,704
But the bond between you
isn't completely broken, is it?

556
00:44:18,675 --> 00:44:21,440
Phob, listen to me.

557
00:44:22,424 --> 00:44:25,320
If one day the two of you

558
00:44:25,816 --> 00:44:28,360
find your way back to each other,

559
00:44:30,344 --> 00:44:33,120
hold on to each other
tightly, just like this.

560
00:44:33,819 --> 00:44:35,664
Don't let go

561
00:44:36,357 --> 00:44:38,539
because of the pain of the past.

562
00:44:39,637 --> 00:44:40,638
Okay?

563
00:44:43,160 --> 00:44:44,161
Yes, Your Highness.

564
00:45:26,200 --> 00:45:27,201
Your Highness!

565
00:45:31,700 --> 00:45:34,040
Your Highness! Your Highness!

566
00:45:36,167 --> 00:45:38,040
Your Highness! Your Highness!

567
00:45:38,595 --> 00:45:40,320
Your Highness! Your Highness!

568
00:45:41,069 --> 00:45:42,480
Your Highness! Your Highness!

569
00:45:43,880 --> 00:45:45,281
[Emergency Room]

570
00:45:55,560 --> 00:45:56,561
Phon?

571
00:45:57,933 --> 00:45:59,160
How is my grandma?

572
00:46:00,080 --> 00:46:01,520
The doctor is still checking on her.

573
00:46:01,880 --> 00:46:03,440
He hasn't come out with the update yet.

574
00:46:07,075 --> 00:46:10,300
What happened to my
mom? What did you do to her?

575
00:46:10,771 --> 00:46:11,772
Dad!

576
00:46:12,371 --> 00:46:14,040
Are you her family? Come with me.

577
00:46:19,619 --> 00:46:20,620
You should go.

578
00:46:21,966 --> 00:46:22,967
Please leave.

579
00:46:54,238 --> 00:46:55,239
Grandma.

580
00:46:56,510 --> 00:46:57,840
How is my mother?

581
00:46:58,350 --> 00:47:01,480
Her kidney condition has
worsened considerably.

582
00:47:01,880 --> 00:47:03,881
She has been very weak for some time,

583
00:47:04,131 --> 00:47:07,100
and this fall has made
her condition even worse.

584
00:47:12,480 --> 00:47:13,680
Is there any way to treat her?

585
00:47:13,918 --> 00:47:17,160
Her kidneys are barely functioning now.

586
00:47:17,491 --> 00:47:19,760
Waste is building up in her blood,

587
00:47:19,971 --> 00:47:22,320
and her body is growing weaker by the day.

588
00:47:22,476 --> 00:47:23,680
As her kidneys fail,

589
00:47:24,048 --> 00:47:27,560
her other organs will
gradually be affected as well.

590
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:31,240
At this point, all we can
do is provide supportive care

591
00:47:31,611 --> 00:47:35,120
and keep her as comfortable as possible.

592
00:48:02,246 --> 00:48:04,280
What did you do to my mom?

593
00:48:05,344 --> 00:48:06,345
I didn't do anything.

594
00:48:06,470 --> 00:48:07,640
Liar!

595
00:48:08,371 --> 00:48:11,200
My mom went to see you,
and she came back like this?!

596
00:48:13,219 --> 00:48:15,520
- It was an accident.
- An accident?

597
00:48:17,100 --> 00:48:18,400
How dare you say that to me?

598
00:48:19,307 --> 00:48:23,000
Haven't you taken enough from me already?

599
00:48:24,422 --> 00:48:25,840
You took my son.

600
00:48:26,539 --> 00:48:29,241
You took my family's trust.

601
00:48:29,571 --> 00:48:30,960
You took my palace,

602
00:48:31,560 --> 00:48:34,250
the honor of my royal house—everything!

603
00:48:35,523 --> 00:48:38,100
And now you're going to
take my mother from me too?!

604
00:48:38,762 --> 00:48:39,763
Huh?

605
00:48:42,613 --> 00:48:43,614
I'm sorry.

606
00:48:44,634 --> 00:48:45,635
You're sorry?

607
00:48:49,211 --> 00:48:52,480
The doctor said her kidneys
have stopped working.

608
00:48:53,397 --> 00:48:56,160
Her other organs will start failing too.

609
00:48:58,198 --> 00:48:59,920
He told us to prepare for the worst.

610
00:50:12,870 --> 00:50:14,100
I've already contacted Chat.

611
00:50:16,100 --> 00:50:18,060
He's coming back from
Nakhon Ratchasima tomorrow.

612
00:50:18,950 --> 00:50:20,270
I'll go meet him when he arrives.

613
00:50:21,568 --> 00:50:22,760
I'm glad he could come.

614
00:50:25,819 --> 00:50:27,200
Grandma must want to see him.

615
00:50:39,982 --> 00:50:42,120
I'm sure Grandma will get better.

616
00:50:43,118 --> 00:50:44,760
She's a strong woman.

617
00:50:47,787 --> 00:50:48,788
It is because of him.

618
00:50:50,747 --> 00:50:53,700
If she hadn't gone out to meet him,
it wouldn't have been like this.

619
00:50:54,598 --> 00:50:56,280
Dad, it was an accident.

620
00:50:58,203 --> 00:50:59,204
It was an accident.

621
00:51:01,638 --> 00:51:02,920
If we still had our palace,

622
00:51:03,632 --> 00:51:05,360
with money and everything,

623
00:51:06,560 --> 00:51:08,560
your grandma wouldn't have been like this.

624
00:51:12,448 --> 00:51:14,560
It is all because of
Phob, that son of a bitch.

625
00:51:30,462 --> 00:51:32,403
Or maybe it's all because of me.

626
00:51:35,694 --> 00:51:36,720
The palace,

627
00:51:38,168 --> 00:51:39,700
our entire family line...

628
00:51:42,104 --> 00:51:44,240
it's all going to come to an end with me.

629
00:51:48,648 --> 00:51:50,920
And now I'm about to lose my mom.

630
00:51:53,958 --> 00:51:55,560
There's nothing I can do.

631
00:51:59,859 --> 00:52:01,800
I've never been able to protect anyone.

632
00:52:48,454 --> 00:52:49,455
Aum.

633
00:52:54,091 --> 00:52:57,317
You should get some rest.
I can stay here with her.

634
00:52:58,800 --> 00:53:00,400
Where is Prince Vasin?

635
00:53:01,320 --> 00:53:04,000
He went to pick up Chat
at Hua Lamphong Station.

636
00:53:05,328 --> 00:53:06,329
They will follow us here.

637
00:53:25,296 --> 00:53:26,297
Grandma.

638
00:53:28,982 --> 00:53:30,768
Chat and Dad will be here soon.

639
00:53:33,214 --> 00:53:34,493
Please wait for them.

640
00:53:45,198 --> 00:53:47,440
Doctor! Doctor!

641
00:53:48,216 --> 00:53:49,560
Doctor! She's awake!

642
00:53:52,974 --> 00:53:53,975
Grandma.

643
00:53:54,920 --> 00:53:55,921
Grandma.

644
00:53:57,608 --> 00:53:58,609
Grandma.

645
00:54:00,029 --> 00:54:01,520
Grandma. Grandma.

646
00:54:01,960 --> 00:54:02,961
Tin, dear.

647
00:54:04,643 --> 00:54:06,520
- Tin.
- Grandma, I am right here.

648
00:54:08,509 --> 00:54:12,160
Such a crybaby, aren't you?

649
00:54:13,102 --> 00:54:14,500
That's not true.

650
00:54:17,070 --> 00:54:19,267
You're still a terrible liar.

651
00:54:21,440 --> 00:54:22,441
Grandma,

652
00:54:23,272 --> 00:54:25,200
please stay strong.

653
00:54:26,035 --> 00:54:27,160
The doctor is coming

654
00:54:27,731 --> 00:54:29,680
and we will go home.

655
00:54:33,904 --> 00:54:35,640
Please don't leave me.

656
00:54:36,192 --> 00:54:37,640
I have no one left.

657
00:54:39,013 --> 00:54:40,720
Who says you have no one left?

658
00:54:41,957 --> 00:54:43,520
Your father's still here.

659
00:54:44,408 --> 00:54:46,120
So are Chat

660
00:54:47,248 --> 00:54:48,649
and Aum.

661
00:54:50,262 --> 00:54:53,663
And the person who loves you…

662
00:54:54,712 --> 00:54:56,260
is still here too.

663
00:54:57,256 --> 00:54:59,760
But I want you here with me.

664
00:55:01,123 --> 00:55:02,160
Tin, dear.

665
00:55:03,659 --> 00:55:05,100
Loss…

666
00:55:06,411 --> 00:55:07,691
is something

667
00:55:09,147 --> 00:55:12,635
none of us can escape.

668
00:55:13,480 --> 00:55:15,200
So while we still have each other,

669
00:55:16,128 --> 00:55:19,000
we should cherish every moment.

670
00:55:24,158 --> 00:55:25,159
Grandma.

671
00:55:25,518 --> 00:55:27,651
Promise me…

672
00:55:29,198 --> 00:55:30,910
you'll be happy.

673
00:55:32,616 --> 00:55:34,560
That you won't be alone,

674
00:55:36,467 --> 00:55:40,080
and you won't close your heart off.

675
00:55:41,363 --> 00:55:43,280
Sure, I promise you.

676
00:55:49,443 --> 00:55:51,520
My good boy.

677
00:55:52,046 --> 00:55:53,047
Grandma.

678
00:55:56,163 --> 00:55:57,360
Grandma.

679
00:56:10,504 --> 00:56:11,505
Grandma.

680
00:56:12,720 --> 00:56:13,721
Grandma.

681
00:56:14,640 --> 00:56:15,641
Grandma.

682
00:56:22,904 --> 00:56:23,905
Grandma.

683
00:56:24,905 --> 00:56:26,760
Grandma, wake up!

684
00:56:28,284 --> 00:56:29,285
Grandma.

685
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:34,640
Don't leave me alone!

686
00:57:08,283 --> 00:57:10,200
May the merit we have made

687
00:57:10,806 --> 00:57:12,998
be dedicated to Princess Patthamapriya.

688
00:57:14,022 --> 00:57:16,560
She was so good to me,

689
00:57:18,174 --> 00:57:21,880
yet I couldn't even be there
to pay my final respects.

690
00:57:38,304 --> 00:57:39,680
I'm sure she would understand.

691
00:57:40,416 --> 00:57:43,440
If we had gone, we would've
only caused more trouble.

692
00:57:49,539 --> 00:57:50,640
I have no idea

693
00:57:52,584 --> 00:57:54,163
how Prince Vasin is holding up.

694
00:57:56,136 --> 00:57:57,256
What about Prince Chatthorn?

695
00:57:58,317 --> 00:57:59,560
And Prince Tinnakorn.

696
00:58:02,243 --> 00:58:04,320
I'm so worried about them, my dear.

697
00:58:34,608 --> 00:58:36,022
Why did this have to happen?

698
00:58:37,478 --> 00:58:38,920
If Grandma hadn't gone to see Phob,

699
00:58:39,966 --> 00:58:41,206
none of this would've happened.

700
00:58:41,363 --> 00:58:42,364
Chat.

701
00:58:43,070 --> 00:58:45,670
It was an accident. Don't you get it,
it was a freaking accident.

702
00:58:49,288 --> 00:58:50,360
An accident?

703
00:58:52,382 --> 00:58:55,896
What good has Phob
ever brought into our lives?

704
00:58:57,000 --> 00:58:58,360
We lost the palace,

705
00:58:59,246 --> 00:59:01,680
our positions, and now Grandmother too.

706
00:59:01,800 --> 00:59:03,320
- It has nothing to do...
- Enough!

707
00:59:11,016 --> 00:59:12,700
This isn't the time to be arguing.

708
00:59:14,728 --> 00:59:17,107
We have far more important things
to deal with right now.

709
00:59:19,800 --> 00:59:20,801
Tinnakorn,

710
00:59:22,414 --> 00:59:24,134
you're coming with me to Nakhon Ratchasima.

711
00:59:25,022 --> 00:59:26,590
Our troops are ready.

712
00:59:27,240 --> 00:59:29,656
Within days, they'll be able to march on
the capital and lay siege to it.

713
00:59:29,680 --> 00:59:30,681
Dad?

714
00:59:31,622 --> 00:59:33,296
We've come this far.

715
00:59:34,059 --> 00:59:35,248
There's no turning back now.

716
00:59:36,900 --> 00:59:38,200
Please, don't do it.

717
00:59:39,478 --> 00:59:40,640
I'm worried about you.

718
00:59:42,062 --> 00:59:43,063
I'm worried about Chat.

719
00:59:46,248 --> 00:59:47,880
We've already lost Grandma.

720
00:59:49,840 --> 00:59:50,841
I can't bear

721
00:59:51,413 --> 00:59:52,920
to lose anyone else.

722
00:59:53,651 --> 00:59:55,640
I've already lost my mother.

723
00:59:57,627 --> 01:00:01,280
This land is all I have left. I'll never
let those people take it from me.

724
01:00:03,760 --> 01:00:05,400
If we don't rise up and fight now,

725
01:00:06,133 --> 01:00:09,480
our land will continue to be violated
with no end in sight.

726
01:00:09,534 --> 01:00:12,960
But Dad, rising up and resorting to force

727
01:00:13,091 --> 01:00:14,867
won't solve anything.

728
01:00:16,003 --> 01:00:18,742
We're all from the same country.
Why can't we just talk this through nicely?

729
01:00:18,766 --> 01:00:20,200
When they seized power,

730
01:00:20,720 --> 01:00:22,400
did they ever try to reason with us?

731
01:00:25,400 --> 01:00:26,401
Hey,

732
01:00:26,835 --> 01:00:28,488
This is our chance.

733
01:00:29,416 --> 01:00:30,720
If we succeed,

734
01:00:31,432 --> 01:00:33,475
we might be able to get everything back.

735
01:00:34,483 --> 01:00:35,484
Chat?

736
01:00:36,131 --> 01:00:37,132
Tinnakorn.

737
01:00:39,037 --> 01:00:40,120
You have to choose now.

738
01:00:41,691 --> 01:00:44,358
Are you on my side or his?

739
01:00:54,643 --> 01:00:56,678
Please don't force me to pick side.

740
01:00:59,341 --> 01:01:00,342
Fine.

741
01:01:01,848 --> 01:01:03,491
It's okay if you can't choose.

742
01:01:04,979 --> 01:01:06,328
But I want you to know this:

743
01:01:07,420 --> 01:01:09,880
if I have to face Phob,

744
01:01:10,680 --> 01:01:12,240
I will not spare his life.

745
01:01:13,603 --> 01:01:14,604
Dad?

746
01:01:15,795 --> 01:01:19,440
Whether for personal
reasons or our opposing beliefs,

747
01:01:20,248 --> 01:01:22,240
there is no way...

748
01:01:22,915 --> 01:01:25,352
Phob and I can live under the same sky.

749
01:01:51,760 --> 01:01:54,637
(Next Episode) Those bastards will have no
place in this land. Will you fight or not?

750
01:01:54,661 --> 01:01:56,250
We will fight!

751
01:01:59,800 --> 01:02:01,360
Can you promise me one thing?

752
01:02:03,214 --> 01:02:05,240
Promise me that you will come back to me.
